{
  "id": "20430_karawomuku",
  "headword": "{殻|から}をむく",
  "reading": "からをむく",
  "romaji": "karawomuku",
  "part_of_speech": "expression, verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to peel; to shell; to husk",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to peel; to shell; to husk; to remove the shell/skin",
      "explanation": "To remove the outer covering of eggs, nuts, shellfish, or other foods with a hard outer layer."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20430_karawomuku_ex1",
      "japanese": "ゆで{卵|たまご}の{殻|から}をむく。",
      "english": "To peel a boiled egg.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20430_karawomuku_ex2",
      "japanese": "エビの{殻|から}をむいてから{炒|いた}める。",
      "english": "Peel the shrimp before stir-frying.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20430_karawomuku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{栗|くり}の{殻|から}をむくのは{大変|たいへん}だけど、{焼|や}き{栗|ぐり}はおいしい。",
      "english": "Peeling chestnuts is hard work, but roasted chestnuts are delicious.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A common cooking expression. The verb むく means to peel or strip off, and {殻|から} refers to any hard outer covering — eggshells, nutshells, crustacean shells, etc.\n\nWHAT CAN BE PEELED:\n- ゆで{卵|たまご}の{殻|から}: boiled egg shell\n- エビの{殻|から}: shrimp shell\n- {栗|くり}の{殻|から}: chestnut shell\n- {落花生|らっかせい}の{殻|から}: peanut shell\n- {貝|かい}の{殻|から}: shellfish shell\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {皮|かわ}をむく: to peel skin (of fruit, vegetables) — for soft outer layers\n- {殻|から}を{割|わ}る: to crack a shell — when breaking rather than peeling\n- {殻|から}を{取|と}る: to remove the shell — more general\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- むく: to peel — the base verb, used with various objects\n- {皮|かわ}をむく: to peel (fruit/vegetables) — for soft coverings like apple skin\n- {殻|から}つき: with shell on, unshelled — describes food still in its shell",
